# clinical v1.19 — WARNING. clinical:category "diagnosis" on a condition.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT VALUE, AND NOT A NONSENSE STRING. "diagnosis" is a real word in
# real clinical documents and it is the wrong word HERE, which is the only kind
# of value that tests a binding rather than testing that enumerations enumerate.
#
# It is the C-CDA vocabulary. A C/CDA Problem Section carries its entries as
# problem observations whose value is typed with words like "diagnosis",
# "problem", "finding", "symptom" and "complaint" — the SNOMED CT problem-type
# concepts the Problem Type value set binds. FHIR R4 Condition.category is a
# DIFFERENT element answering a DIFFERENT question: not "what kind of clinical
# statement is this" but "where does this condition live in the chart", with
# exactly two codes, problem-list-item and encounter-diagnosis
# (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/valueset-condition-category.html).
#
# So this is the confusion the binding exists to catch: a converter reading a
# C-CDA problem observation and copying its type word straight into
# Condition.category produces exactly this record. The word looks like a
# category, it is spelled correctly, and it means something real — it is simply
# an answer to the other question. "encounter-diagnosis" is the code it would
# have to be mapped to if the source meant a diagnosis made at a visit, and
# nothing in the string itself says whether it did.
#
# A nonsense value would have proved only that sh:in is enumerated. This one
# proves the two vocabularies are distinguished.
#
# sh:Warning, not sh:Violation, per the core v3.5 ratchet: this is the first
# release to bind clinical:category on any shape and pods may already carry it.
# Nothing rejects this record, and the fixture asserts exactly that alongside
# the warning. The binding is also FHIR-extensible rather than required, which
# is a second reason the severity is Warning and not Violation.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:c0nd0119-0000-4000-8000-000000000003> a health:ConditionRecord ;
    health:conditionName "Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus" ;
    health:status "active" ;
    health:onsetDate "2021-08-19T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    clinical:category "diagnosis" ;
    health:icd10Code <http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10-cm/E11.9> ;
    health:snomedCode <http://snomed.info/sct/44054006> ;
    health:conditionClass "endocrine" ;
    health:sourceRecordId "ehr-cond-2021-0819-001" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
